---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="How it works · Mental Note" active="how-it-works">
<div class="phead"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="eyebrow">How this works</div>
  <h1>What happens after you hit send.</h1>
  <p class="lead">No account, no email, no name required. Here is the whole process, so nothing about it is a surprise.</p>
</div></div>
<div class="light"><div class="block" style="padding-top:56px"><div class="wrap rv">
  <ol class="steps">
    <li><span class="num">01</span><div><h3>You write it</h3><p>No account, no name. You can add your email if you want the articles and event invites — it's stored separately and never attached to what you wrote.</p></div></li>
    <li><span class="num">02</span><div><h3>One of us reads it</h3><p>Both founders read every note before anything goes up. Usually within a day.</p></div></li>
    <li><span class="num">03</span><div><h3>It gets published, or it doesn't</h3><p>We don't publish notes describing methods of self-harm, or anything that identifies someone. Everything else goes up.</p><span class="flag">Human decision, never automatic</span></div></li>
    <li><span class="num">04</span><div><h3>Someone else finds it</h3><p>It joins the wall for that month, and stays in the archive after.</p></div></li>
  </ol>
</div></div>

<div class="block" style="padding-top:0"><div class="wrap rv">
  <div class="eyebrow">Before you write anything</div>
  <h2>The answers you'd want shouldn't be buried.</h2>
  <dl class="qa">
    <div><dt>Who reads my note?</dt><dd>The two of us. Nobody else, and no software deciding for us.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Is it actually anonymous?</dt><dd>Yes. Notes carry no name and no account. If you give us your email for the newsletter, it lives in a separate list and is never linked to a note.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>What if I'm struggling right now?</dt><dd>A note isn't help. Call or text 988, or text HOME to 741741 — that's a real person, right now.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>What do you do with my check-ins?</dt><dd>Nothing. They stay on your phone. We never see them.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Are you qualified?</dt><dd>No, and we say so everywhere. We're students who write about this, not clinicians.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>How do you pay for this?</dt><dd>School talks and donations. No ads, ever.</dd></div>
  </dl>
  <div class="acts" style="margin-top:44px"><a class="b1 dk" href="/this-week">Write a note</a></div>
</div></div></div>
</Layout>
